      "message": "This change is low risk for the current repository. The only thing worth flagging is the implementation/commit-message mismatch around None vs falsy values at if not ssh_port:. \n\nIf you want strict signature semantics, that line should use is None; otherwise the repository-wide impact remains non-breaking.\n\nif not ssh_port: treats all falsy values as “missing”:\n```\nNone\n\"\"\n0\nFalse\n```\nif ssh_port is None: treats only None as “missing”.\nSo if the commit says “When ssh_port is None, use ${SSH_PORT}”, then the precise implementation should be:\n\n```\nif ssh_port is None:\n    ssh_port \u003d BuiltIn().get_variable_value(\"${SSH_PORT}\", default\u003d\"22\")\n```",
